[470.398086, "o", "\u001b[38;5;208m● belay\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[470.398283, "o", "  Both saved to the yearly bank. Small heads-up: today's the 24th, so **car insurance is due this month** — worth checking it's already gone out or budgeted for.\r\n\r\n  Now, mode. Three ways to run this:\r\n\r\n  - **Awareness** — see where money goes, no strict limits. Lightest touch.\r\n  - **Envelopes** — hard caps per category (groceries, dining, etc.), enforced.\r\n  - **Hybrid** — awareness overall, envelopes only for a category or two that need containing.\r\n\r\n  Your history doesn't show any envelope-style structure already in place (no sub-account splits, no systematic caps) — just one steady account with a card refilled as needed. So I'd start with **awareness**: track and see clearly first, add structure later only where the data says you need it.\r\n\r\n  Two questions:\r\n  1. Awareness sound right to start, or do you already know a category you want capped (e.g. dining out, groceries)?\r\n  2. Any savings goal to track — an amount, a target, or just \"build a buffer\"?\r\n\r\n\u001b[1;36malex ▸ \u001b[0m"]
