[715.1031, "o", "\u001b[38;5;208m● belay\u001b[0m\r\n  Onboarding's done. Here's where things landed:\r\n\r\n  **Workspace built:** 2 accounts ingested (427 transactions total, clean), 96 transfer pairs matched (card top-ups excluded from spend), 8 merchant patterns confirmed, 2 yearly items, awareness mode with a €1,503.96 buffer goal, and August's budget drafted and exported to Excel.\r\n\r\n  **August 2026 draft** (`finance/months/2026-08/reports/budget_2026-08.xlsx`):\r\n  - Income: €2,800\r\n  - Groceries ~€298, Car ~€73, Subscriptions ~€26, Dining out ~€26 (awareness targets, not caps)\r\n  - Savings: ~€2,378 toward the buffer\r\n\r\n  One thing worth knowing: the auto-draft tool's 3-month lookback would have quietly used July (which doesn't exist yet — we're mid-month) as a zero month, deflating every number by about a third. I caught it and recomputed from the three complete months instead, so what's in the file is correct.\r\n\r\n  **Monthly rhythm going forward:** drop new bank exports in `finance/inbox/` and run `/reconcile-month` around month-end to see how things actually went; run `/monthly-prep` a few days before the next month starts to draft its budget the same way.\r\n\r\n"]
[715.103155, "o", "\u001b[1;36malex ▸ \u001b[0m"]
